The main real gap is server-to-client campfire block-entity synchronization: vanilla’s `placeFood`, `cookTick`, and `getUpdateTag` update/send the campfire contents immediately, while Pumpkin had persistence and cooking but no `chunk_data_nbt` payload for live updates. I also found a smaller ItemEntity parity bug: `setPickUpDelay` left Pumpkin’s internal “never pick up” flag set, unlike vanilla’s single-field implementation. I’m patching both, with focused tests for the campfire payload and delay-state transition.
