codex
A second concrete gap surfaced in the same audit: `onDataChanged` ultimately matters because Pumpkin only emits/saves dirty block entities, while both sensor entities currently have the default “never dirty” implementation. I’m adding atomic dirty tracking when the persisted vibration frequency changes, including the calibrated variant, and a small unit test for the state transition.
