The worklist contains two classes. Lectern’s missing names mostly map cleanly to generated block-state tables or existing hooks (`use_with_item`, `normal_use`, `pulse`, `set_has_book`). Sign editing is the stronger genuine gap: the current packet path mutates raw lines directly, without vanilla’s update/dirty semantics or editor-distance cleanup. I’m tracing the existing block-entity tick/update APIs now so the patch fits the server’s lifecycle.
