codex
I found two server-observable gaps worth shipping: decorated-pot insertion was comparing only item IDs and hard-coding a 64-stack cap, while vanilla requires identical components and the item’s max stack size; iron golem step sounds were not wired into the shared grounded-movement hook. I’ll also synchronize the golem’s attack animation timer when its renamed `try_attack` path broadcasts vanilla event 4.
