codex
I found two additional concrete server-state gaps in the same class while checking the vanilla save contract: `VillagerDataFinalized` and `Xp` are written/read by vanilla but were not persisted by Pumpkin. I’m adding those fields and accessors, carrying XP into the cured villager, and synchronizing villager metadata through the existing metadata path. Gossip/trade methods remain covered by the existing cure path/state model because this Rust implementation has no villager-to-zombie infection caller.
apply patch
