     1	// Legacy invariant checks retained for vanilla behavior; migrate these paths before removing this allow.
     2	#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic)]
     3	// Port of net.minecraft.world.entity.monster.warden.{Warden, WardenAi} plus
     4	// net.minecraft.world.entity.ai.behavior.warden.SonicBoom, using the anger-system port in
     5	// `warden_anger.rs` and the GameEvent/vibration engine in `crate::world::game_event`.
     6	//
     7	// Pumpkin has no Brain/Memory/Activity system (see PARITY.md), so `WardenAi`'s activity
     8	// ladder (EMERGE/DIG/ROAR/FIGHT/INVESTIGATE/SNIFF/IDLE, each a `Brain` memory-gated
     9	// `Behavior` list) is not portable as-is. This implementation instead keeps the anger
    10	// state and cooldowns as plain fields on `WardenEntity`, ticked directly from `mob_tick`,
    11	// and drives targeting/attacking through the existing Goal system. Concretely ported:
    12	// anger accumulation from vibrations and melee hits, vibration-driven investigation
    13	// (via `mob_entity.target`), and the sonic boom ranged attack. Explicitly NOT ported,
    14	// with reasons:
    15	//
    16	// - Pose-driven emerge/dig/roar/sniff animation states (Warden.java lines 275-282,
    17	//   346-365, 517-521, `AnimationState` fields): Pumpkin's `Entity` DOES have a `Pose`
    18	//   concept (`pumpkin_data::entity::EntityPose`, `Entity::pose` + `Entity::set_pose`,
    19	//   already used by Breeze/Frog/Villager/EnderPearl) generated with `Roaring`,
    20	//   `Sniffing`, `Emerging`, `Digging` variants matching vanilla's `Pose` enum 1:1 — an
    21	//   earlier version of this comment claiming otherwise was wrong. What's actually
    22	//   missing is vanilla's Brain/Memory/Activity ladder that decides *when* to enter each
    23	//   pose (`WardenAi.getActivities`/`updateActivity`, `SetRoarTarget`, `TryToSniff`,
    24	//   `DIG_COOLDOWN`/`ROAR_TARGET`/`IS_SNIFFING` memories) — see the top-of-file note above
    25	//   on why that framework isn't portable as-is. Of the four poses:
    26	//   - ROARING is ported below (`start_roar`/`cancel_roar`, ticked in `mob_tick`): fully
    27	//     timer-driven (`WardenAi.ROAR_DURATION` = 84 ticks, sound at tick 25 per
    28	//     `Roar.TICKS_BEFORE_PLAYING_ROAR_SOUND`), so it needs no memory/sensor equivalent.
    29	//     It replaces the previous immediate `set_attack_target` call on becoming angry at a
    30	//     player with vanilla's actual behavior (`Warden.increaseAngerAt` only *erases* the
    31	//     attack target on that transition; it's `Roar.stop()` that assigns the roar target as
    32	//     the new attack target once the roar finishes, Roar.java:58-65).
    33	//   - EMERGING (`Warden.finalizeSpawn`, Warden.java:480-492) is gated on
    34	//     `EntitySpawnReason::TRIGGERED` (sculk shrieker summons only) in vanilla. Pumpkin has
    35	//     no spawn-reason plumbing at all (`grep EntitySpawnReason pumpkin/src/` turns up only
    36	//     TODOs, e.g. `mob/mod.rs:978`), so there's no way to tell a triggered summon from a
    37	//     natural/`/summon` spawn here — NOT implemented, left for when spawn-reason exists,
    38	//     to avoid a visible regression (emerging on every spawn).
    39	//   - DIGGING and SNIFFING are NOT implemented: both are gated on Brain sensors Pumpkin
    40	//     has no equivalent for (`NEAREST_ATTACKABLE`, `DISTURBANCE_LOCATION` absence for
    41	//     Sniffing's `TryToSniff`; `DIG_COOLDOWN`/`ROAR_TARGET` absence for Digging), and
    42	//     Digging in particular ends in `body.remove(Entity.RemovalReason.DISCARDED)`
    43	//     (`Digging.java:36-40`) — an under-specified port here would despawn Wardens
    44	//     unexpectedly, which is a worse regression than the missing animation. Left as a
    45	//     separate, reviewed follow-up.
    46	//   Temporary invulnerability while emerging (`isInvulnerableTo`, Warden.java:161-163) IS
    47	//   implemented, as `pre_damage` below - EMERGING is reachable now via `start_emerging`.
    48	//   `ignoreExplosion` (Warden.java:367-370) IS implemented, as the WARDEN arm of
    49	//   `EntityBase::ignores_explosion`: the explosion loop skips the entity outright, so that
    50	//   one check covers the knockback half as well as the damage half.
    51	//   `getDefaultDimensions` (Warden.java:516-521) IS implemented, as the WARDEN arm of
    52	//   `Entity::get_default_dimensions`, applied by `sync_warden_pose` below.
    53	//   `isPushable` (Warden.java:523-526) is NOT, and needs no code: mobs reach
    54	//   `EntityBase::is_pushable`, whose default is `false` for every mob in this codebase, so an
