     4	//!
     5	//! This is the load-bearing bridge between brain memory and the movement stack: it is the only
     6	//! reader of `WALK_TARGET`, and every behavior that wants the mob to go somewhere does it by
     7	//! writing that memory and letting this sink drain it into `Navigator`.
     8	//!
     9	//! # Deviations from vanilla, and why
    10	//!
    11	//! Vanilla's version is built on `PathNavigation.createPath(pos, 0)` returning a `Path` object
    12	//! that the behavior stores, tests with `canReach()`, publishes into `MemoryModuleType.PATH`,
    13	//! and finally hands to `moveTo(path, speed)` (`MoveToTargetSink.java:92-93,113-140`).
    14	//! Pumpkin's `Navigator` has no such API: the only entry point is
    15	//! `set_progress(NavigatorGoal::new(from, to, speed))` (`ai/pathfinder/mod.rs:101-105`), and the
    16	//! path is computed lazily inside `Navigator::tick` (`ai/pathfinder/mod.rs:339-345`). So:
    17	//!
    18	//! - `MemoryModuleType.PATH` is not represented, and is dropped from the entry condition.
    19	//!   Vanilla uses `PATH` `VALUE_ABSENT` to stop the sink restarting while a path is live; the
    20	//!   replacement guard is `Navigator::is_idle()` in `can_still_use`.
    21	//! - `CANT_REACH_WALK_TARGET_SINCE` stays in the entry condition as `REGISTERED` and is erased on
    22	//!   reaching the target, but is never *set*: it is only written from vanilla's
    23	//!   `path.canReach()` branch, and Pumpkin cannot answer that question before the navigator has
    24	//!   run. Nothing in this stage reads it.
    25	//! - The `DefaultRandomPos.getPosTowards` partial-step fallback (`:132-136`) is not ported --
    26	//!   Pumpkin's navigator already degrades to a best-effort partial path internally
    27	//!   (`ai/pathfinder/mod.rs:266-292` returns the best node reached even when `reached == false`).
    28	//! - `stop`'s `remainingCooldown = random.nextInt(40)` is gated on
    29	//!   `body.getNavigation().isStuck()` (`:79-83`), which Pumpkin's `Navigator` does not expose.
    30	//!   The cooldown field and its `checkExtraStartConditions` drain are kept so the shape is
    31	//!   right, but nothing currently sets it.
    32	
