     3	// Port of net.minecraft.world.entity.animal.allay.{Allay, AllayAi}.
     4	//
     5	// This is Stage 2 of `BRAIN_DESIGN.md`: the Allay is the first mob in this codebase driven by
     6	// `crate::entity::ai::brain` rather than by the Goal system, matching vanilla, where `Allay`
     7	// has no `goalSelector` entries at all and `AllayAi.getActivities()` (`AllayAi.java:57-59`)
     8	// supplies a CORE and an IDLE activity. The previous revision of this file carried
     9	// `LIKED_PLAYER` / `LIKED_NOTEBLOCK_POSITION` / `LIKED_NOTEBLOCK_COOLDOWN_TICKS` as plain
    10	// fields and had no item-fetch loop at all; those three are now real brain memories and the
    11	// fetch loop is the vanilla behavior set.
    12	//
    13	// Concretely ported: the CORE activity (`AllayAi.java:61-73`) and the IDLE activity
    14	// (`AllayAi.java:75-90`) minus `SetEntityLookTargetSometimes`, the item give/take/duplicate
    15	// `mobInteract` branch (`Allay.java:281-317`), jukebox/note-block dancing
    16	// (`setJukeboxPlaying`, `hearNoteblock`, `shouldStopDancing`), the duplication cooldown, and
    17	// the `wantsToPickUp`/`canPickUpLoot`/`pickUpItem` inventory path (`Allay.java:263-362`).
    18	//
    19	// Explicitly NOT ported, with reasons:
    20	//
    21	// - `SetEntityLookTargetSometimes.create(6.0F, UniformInt.of(30, 60))` (`AllayAi.java:85`).
    22	//   It reads `NEAREST_VISIBLE_LIVING_ENTITIES`, which needs a `NearestLivingEntitiesSensor`;
    23	//   only `NearestItemSensor` is ported (`ai/brain/sensor/`). An Allay therefore does not
    24	//   glance at nearby players while idling. `SetWalkTargetFromLookTarget` in the `RunOne` is
    25	//   kept, but with nothing writing `LOOK_TARGET` from the world it only ever follows a look
    26	//   target some other behavior set.
    27	// - `DATA_DANCING`/`DATA_CAN_DUPLICATE` client-synced booleans and the client-side
    28	//   `holdingItemAnimationTicks`/`dancingAnimationTicks`/`spinningAnimationTicks` animation
    29	//   state (`Allay.java:80-81, 228-260, 393-404`): Pumpkin's `Entity` has no generic boolean
    30	//   tracked-data slot exposed to per-mob code the way vanilla's `SynchedEntityData.Builder`
    31	//   does, and no client animation-state channel at all (the same gap `warden.rs` notes for
    32	//   `AnimationState`). `is_dancing` below is server-side only.
    33	// - `hasNonMatchingPotion` (`Allay.java:353-358`), which compares
    34	//   `DataComponents.POTION_CONTENTS`: the item-identity half of `allayConsidersItemEqual` is
    35	//   ported, the potion-content special case is not, so an Allay holding a healing potion will
    36	//   also fetch a poison potion.
    37	// - `CriteriaTriggers.ALLAY_DROP_ITEM_ON_BLOCK` in `AllayAi.onItemThrown` (`AllayAi.java:159`):
    38	//   no advancement trigger of that name is wired up here.
    39	// - `Allay.getPickupReach()` (`Allay.java:336-339`), a custom pickup box. The shared
    40	//   `Mob::mob_try_pick_up_items` pass uses its own reach and is not parameterised.
    41	//
    42	// Two deviations worth naming because they are structural, not omissions:
    43	//
    44	// - The main-hand item is mirrored into a plain `std::sync::Mutex<ItemStack>`. Vanilla reads
