codex
The selector leads are all represented by existing parser state, flags, option variants, and macro-backed setters; there is no selector implementation gap to ship. In `HappyGhast`, fall-damage suppression is already inlined in the shared living tick, while the fixed vanilla voice pitch is genuinely missing from the `Mob` override path. I’m adding that override plus a direct fall-damage guard at the existing mob hook, with focused pure tests.
